WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.970
Now, the gods are on my side.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.700
A silver badge.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.430
Are those Mongol letters?

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.600
Listen, Shiraishi. 
I wanted to ask you something.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.400
Why are you risking death here?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:16.950
There's nothing in it for you.

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.710
Well... It just ended up that way, I guess.

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:24.630
I felt like I had to do something 
after watching the islanders

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.010
get slaughtered by the Mongol armies.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.250
Shiraishi, let's be honest with each other.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.530
What are you trying to say?

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.750
I'm asking you if you're
really okay with this.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.570
If you still have any pride as a samurai,

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.770
then you shouldn't sell 
your services for free.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.650
You need to fight for a reward.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.740
Let me hear you out.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:25.410
There are people who aren't in the 
Toibarai who know about this castle.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.970
And we just killed a shit ton of Mongols.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.790
They'll find us. It's certain.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.300
We can't stay here.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.710
We need to get as far away 
from the Mongols as we possibly can.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.710
Do what you want,

00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:42.220
but we won't abandon this place.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.240
This castle and the villages along the coast,

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.360
make up the land where 
Toibarai's ancestors' souls dwell.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.600
The soldiers' morale will fail them 
if they try to fight anywhere else.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:56.430
Fighting here is what 
will give us the advantage.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.600
I see. So that's it.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.000
You didn't take in all those people 
from the capital and Sasu

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.990
just because of the Emperor's 
orders or your ancestor's words.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.050
You wanted as many extra men 
as possible to protect this place.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.740
If you want to leave, we won't stop you.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.430
But even if you can escape the Mongols,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.250
can you survive General Winter?

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:28.070
Alone in the wilderness with 
 nothing but the clothes on your back,

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:31.480
all you'll find is hunger and the cold.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:36.430
We're not telling you to fight here.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:42.950
Just stay inside the strong stone walls, 
and wait for them to pass.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:47.390
Wait!

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:48.290
Leave him.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:02.110
Hey, I heard you told the Magistrate 
to abandon the castle.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.860
You're not even from this island, exile.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:06.880
Don't try to tell us what to do.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:15.550
Hey, I heard you're good at some sword 
style called "Gikei style," right?

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.610
Can you give us a lesson with this stick?

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.510
No need for that.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.900
I'll fight you with this.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:26.150
Bastard!

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:33.790
That's not a sword!

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.360
If you want to die, I can use that stick.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.290
Gikei style is...

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.140
...a style used to kill.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.580
Then kill me!

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:52.760
All of us would be glad to die 
in the land of our ancestors!

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.800
I'll do the best I can to protect it!

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.060
Okay, how about this?

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.290
I'll fight you all at once.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.770
If you all lose, show me 
your faces and tell me your names.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.610
Hey, Kuchii and the Toibarai are fighting!

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.380
What?

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.050
The exile from the capital started a fight!

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.660
Let's join in!

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:22.930
Come and get us!

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:24.550
You want to fight, asshole?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:25.840
The hell you say?

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.620
Get out of here! Damn it!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.900
Hey, what's all this about?

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.390
They just asked me for a sparring match.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.640
Now, take off your helmets 
and give me your names.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.630
Fine. We promised we would.

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.310
Nakamaru of Mitsuka.

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:42.310
Kamaami.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.380
Jirou.

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:44.240
Tasuke.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.150
Will the rest of you take off your 
masks and give me your names, as well?

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.230
What?

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:53.210
If we do have to fight the Mongols here,

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:57.110
can you entrust your lives to people 
whose faces and names you don't know?

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:01.570
So, Kuchii Jinzaburou,

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:06.820
if we do have to fight the Mongols here,

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:09.050
will you stay in the castle?

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.300
I owe you a debt from yesterday.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:16.640
And this is the place where you'll 
really do the best you can, right?

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:18.810
I guess I've got no choice 
but to help you, then.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.600
Maybe it was wrong to try and 
give up on a place to protect people,

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:26.270
instead of trying to protect 
both the people and a place.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:32.310
If you stay here, you'll really be able 
to show me all you've got, right?

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:35.320
Of course.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:38.830
But if you just use these walls to hide,

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:41.120
they won't protect you 
when you need them most.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:44.030
I'm going to strengthen 
the castle's defenses.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.540
You don't need to tell us that.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.630
Two days ago,

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:57.170
I left Sasu Valley and arrived 
at a small fishing village.

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:59.510
I was invited to the house 
of a certain family...

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:06.240
But for some reason, 
the villagers attacked me.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:09.230
I was captured.

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.710
And then the Mongol soldiers arrived.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.830
I thought it was over for sure that time...

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:21.770
But this Mongol general 
named Nergui or something...

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:25.070
He seemed to realize my potential.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:29.780
This is a Mongol pass he gave me.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:32.090
I can go to meet him any time I want.

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:34.050
So you're a traitor?

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.420
That's a nasty way to put it.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:41.090
Our job is to fight for a liege 
in exchange for the lands he lets us have.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:47.850
Whether that liege is Japanese 
or Mongol makes no difference.

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.050
How about it, Shiraishi?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.430
We can serve the Mongol army 
and win glory for ourselves,

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.990
receive lands from the Mongol general,

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:58.430
and go back to being landed lords!

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.160
Damn it all!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:05.080
<b>Uriyan Edei's Army 
Funbishi</b>

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.080
Where the hell did those Japanese escape to?

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.680
I have men looking for them,

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:10.800
<b>Uriyan Edei's Army 
Ochirubato</b>

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.610
but these mountains are bigger than they look.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.790
They're the perfect place 
for those monkeys to hide.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.250
It's not like they 
disappeared into thin air.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.090
<b>Uriyan Edei's Army
Choukuru</b>

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.100
Are there no traces at all?

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:18.000
Let's just ignore the islanders.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:18.760
What?

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:24.010
There are only a few days until the time 
the priests have told us to leave port.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.230
I believe our best choice is to let

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:29.220
the soldiers rest before we 
continue our conquest of Japan.

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:31.600
So we give up?

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.950
Impossible!

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:35.310
That's what the Japanese want us to do.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:42.500
Yes. If we don't know where they are, 
there's nothing we can do.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.830
We'll call off the pursuit.

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:44.940
Shit!

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:50.680
<i>I guess I won't get that girl 
I was looking forward to, huh?</i>

00:08:51.620 --> 00:08:53.510
If I may, General...

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:55.300
What is it, Nergui?

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.090
While you were gone,

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:01.530
I convinced several 
of the islanders to act as spies,

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:03.380
and spread them throughout the island.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:06.030
If we're lucky,

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:09.120
they might tell us where our foes 
are hiding as soon as today.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.700
That changes things.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:19.880
Our commanders have given us 
the capital, the best meal on the island.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:25.160
We need to make sure we suck it 
down to the marrow of its bones,

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.760
or it just wouldn't feel right, would it?

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:30.120
What do you think, Shiraishi?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.290
It's not a bad deal, is it?

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:35.350
They might make us governors if we're lucky!

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:40.110
Why are you so worried?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:42.260
Do we have anything left to lose?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.270
We do.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:53.100
I don't want to lose my soul, as well.

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:56.090
I appreciate the offer, 
but I can't betray everyone.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:01.630
Sheesh... My brother was the same way.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.550
"Duty." "Soul."

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:05.850
While he was fretting and worrying,

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.860
someone else took the initiative, and he died.

00:10:07.860 --> 00:10:10.780
And that someone was me!

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.300
You're an exile. 
It's the same for you, right?

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.300
Is your soul so wonderful 
you'd miss it if you lost it?

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.090
Enough, Obusuma.

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:25.380
I'll let you go, just this once.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:26.630
Go.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.970
How nice of you.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:32.850
I owe you one!

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.690
I knew exactly what you'd do.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:47.280
Damn it...

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:53.930
Why did you kill him, mister?

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.940
You're one of the divers from before?

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.180
Look.

00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:00.640
He was working with the Mongols.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.360
A traitor?

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.670
But I didn't need to kill him.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:11.300
No, you did the only thing you could do!

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.430
I'll tell everyone for you!

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.680
I'll go bring someone.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.470
Wait.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.730
What? Mis—

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.340
Why?

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:47.110
I'm sorry.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:54.080
I-I changed my mind about you.

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:08.610
Obusuma Saburou...

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:10.660
I can work with the Mongols,

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.130
but not with scum like you!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:29.770
Chikuzen Dazaifu Magistrate Fortress

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.090
How goes the loading of the ships?

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.010
It will take more time.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.140
Get as many ships as you can,

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:38.550
loaded with all the arrows 
and provisions you can find.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.530
And then we need 
as many troops as we can get.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:46.530
Once they're here, we'll have them 
board and head for Tsushima!

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:54.730
<i>There are people out there who
 will fight for men they've never met...</i>

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:56.910
<i>Just wait,</i>

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.240
<i>Kuchii Jinzaburou.</i>

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:05.850
Jinzaburou!

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:09.350
I want your honest opinion.

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.810
Are reinforcements coming? Or not?

00:13:14.920 --> 00:13:17.430
I'm sending 3,000 soldiers to Tsushima.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:18.980
They are.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.200
He'll keep his promise.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.530
A samurai always does.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:27.940
He said he'll send reinforcements, 
and now he has to.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.900
The Shouni Clan are duty-bound 
to defend Tsushima.

00:13:32.570 --> 00:13:33.910
I see.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:36.920
That's rare...

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.420
You're never optimistic.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.210
But we don't know 
for sure that they'll come.

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:44.640
So stay sharp.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:51.250
<i>Just the promise of reinforcements 
is keeping everyone's spirits up.</i>

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:54.940
<i>But... I don't know if it's 
really going to happen.</i>

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:58.460
<i>They would have the terrain advantage 
if they fought the Mongols at Kyushu.</i>

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:04.010
<i>I can't believe they'd abandon it and 
send their troops across dangerous seas.</i>

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:08.860
<i>But if reinforcements do come...</i>

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.280
<i>It means we can do more, but...</i>

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.820
Onami-chan!

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.800
How horrible...

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.130
It's my fault.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.290
I should've come sooner.

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:28.980
From the look of things, it would've 
been too late, even if you had.

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.130
Magistrate...

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:31.880
What was the cause of death?

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:36.830
This piece of shit samurai must 
have tried to rape Onami!

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.760
But she fought back and killed him, too!

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.940
He tried to put his hands on other 
women, and nobody liked him!

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:48.270
Is something wrong, Magistrate?

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:52.020
No.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.530
Let's bury Nami.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.190
Obusuma Saburou is dead?

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:58.370
Yeah.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:15:01.020
He and one of the diving 
women killed each other.

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.500
What happened?

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:05.550
No idea. Maybe he grabbed her butt?

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.810
Loser.

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.520
That's terrifying...

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:12.210
I need to be careful around those women, too.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:16.850
<i>He looked like a decently skilled warrior...</i>

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.220
<i>It's odd that he'd be killed so easily...</i>

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.960
I guess we should go bury him.

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:26.900
We all fought on the same 
battlefield two days ago.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:30.380
Hey, where's Shiraishi-dono?

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:31.770
No idea.

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.030
He missed dinner, 
and I haven't seen him since.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:48.330
So there's a castle in the 
mountains on the north side?

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:53.350
And the escaped islanders are hiding there?

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.260
That's good to know.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:16:00.150
General, this silver badge is real, 
but we can't trust him.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:03.350
This isn't the man I gave it to.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.560
The safe thing to do would be to kill him.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.110
You said your name was Shiraishi?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:15.370
Your reward will be dependent 
on what you do now.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.380
It's dependent on what you do now.

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:20.950
So you'll trust me, then?

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:24.710
I want to keep as many 
of my soldiers alive as possible.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:27.250
Help me out with that.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:31.690
First, can you tell me the 
weaknesses of that castle?

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.760
Do they have enough defenders?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:44.120
They don't have enough defenders 
to protect a castle that size, I think.

00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:46.400
I see.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.980
So if we concentrate our forces 
on a single point of attack,

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:53.060
the other points will 
become undefended, huh?

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:56.230
It's possible.

00:16:56.230 --> 00:17:01.250
So, are there a lot of things 
to plunder in the castle?

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:05.430
Provisions, weapons, cloth, treasure...

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.750
And more than anything, slaves!

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:11.400
Especially the women and children.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.460
Only if we can take them alive, though.

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:18.750
<i>I shudder to think of the 
terrible thing I've done,</i>

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:22.020
<i>but I can't turn back now.</i>

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.630
Yeah, there's plenty.

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:28.390
There's tons of treasure 
inside that mountain.

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:31.430
<i>If I've already betrayed them, 
I may as well keep doing it!</i>

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:36.920
Karaun, did you see that 
expression he had for a moment?

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.610
An expression of pain.

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.260
And it was real.

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:45.200
The face of someone who betrayed 
his comrades and is overcome with guilt.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:47.830
That's the face of a true traitor.

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:52.560
And anyone without that sense 
of guilt can't be trusted.

00:17:54.090 --> 00:17:57.310
The Mongols prize those 
who agree to serve us willingly.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:01.090
You were the first Japanese 
to surrender to us.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:04.050
And you will receive 
the best treatment of them.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.310
Now, my new Japanese friend,

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:09.090
you may split the spoils with me.

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:15.770
This is sulfur.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:19.790
If you cover a stick with it, 
you can use it to easily start fires.

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.650
It stinks.

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:25.070
If they got it locally, 
it's probably from Iwo Jima.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:27.200
It's usually used as medicine, right?

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.410
I'd like some later.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.910
By the way, it seems 
we're missing some exiles.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:41.290
That big one...

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:45.410
Oh, I haven't seen Shiraishi 
since this afternoon.

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:47.040
This afternoon?

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.460
Nobody saw him?

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.650
What's on your mind?

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:54.500
I'll come out and say it.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:57.660
I'm thinking his disappearance 
might have something

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:01.360
to do with the death 
of a man named Obusuma.

00:19:01.810 --> 00:19:03.330
What do you mean?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:06.580
The man's collarbone 
had been sliced clean through.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.130
The short katanas the women 
carry couldn't do that.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:13.740
It was a tachi katana...

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.420
Hey, everyone.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.830
Shiraishi! Where were you?

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.350
I was following this thing.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.840
That's a huge boar.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:29.980
Nice work!

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:33.100
It was tough.

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:39.550
I'm happy to get a chance 
to rest by the fire.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.650
We haven't had time until now.

00:19:42.530 --> 00:19:44.910
You guys are like a bunch of old geezers.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.820
We've got no drink, and I'm bored!

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.820
Somebody sing!

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.580
Yes...

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.640
It doesn't have to be loud. Someone sing.

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.340
Kano, how about you?

00:19:57.800 --> 00:19:59.980
A cheerful song.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:04.140
Something that would help us feel like 
we made it through the day, and sleep...

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:06.960
But I'm just a guard...

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:11.270
It's our job to bring peace 
to the princess's heart.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:15.040
How about we sing one of the hayauta 
songs we learned as children?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:17.150
I'll sing the sue part.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.050
You honor me too highly, Princess.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:20.990
Give it up, Kano.

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:28.580
All right. I can't promise 
it will be any good, but...

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:39.080
Where is the branch I shall rest on tonight?

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:47.080
It's far ahead, beyond the mountains.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:55.090
A kotsuzura tree deep in the mountains.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:59.810
Hmph! I know a more elegant song than this.

00:20:55.870 --> 00:21:03.230
A kotsuzura tree as the sun sets...

00:20:59.810 --> 00:21:04.110
I'm sure you do, 
but I'd rather they sing than you.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:11.620
Grab on to the heron's neck...

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:20.450
It's so long, so very long...

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:30.920
Hey, look! Smoke signals!

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:36.250
The Mongols are coming?

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:38.300
They found this place?

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.640
I don't know.

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:42.230
But they're heading straight here.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:45.700
They'll reach Kanatanoki 
Castle this afternoon.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:49.470
<i>So they're here...</i>

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:54.980
<i>Now that the Mongols had a target, 
they marched straight for it.</i>

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:58.560
<i>Their march was filled with confidence.</i>

00:22:00.910 --> 00:22:05.830
<i>The battle of Kanatanoki Castle had begun.</i>

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.010
<b>Episode 08:
Betrayer's Strike</b>
